{
	"findings": [
		"Keywords and storage are error red (red.3 / red.5), the most frequent colored token, so red no longer means 'wrong' and invalid code blends in.",
		"Tags, JSON keys, markdown quotes and regex escapes are green, which collides with added/success.",
		"Body text is the brightest thing on the page (#e6edf3, 16:1 dark; #1f2328, 14.8:1 light), so plain identifiers glare and every colored token looks recessive.",
		"No landmarks: declarations and uses share one color (entity.name.function, entity.name), and only markdown headings are bold.",
		"Hue is spent on body text: `variable` is orange and `variable.other.constant` blue, so a const name changes color between declaration and use.",
		"Blue is overloaded: strings, constants, support, property names, `this`, headings, inline code, diff headers and output all share it.",
		"Light comments (gray.5) fall to 4.3:1 on the gray.0 background, and punctuation, operators and import plumbing get no rules at all, so they inherit full-strength body text.",
		"Missing scopes: keyword.operator, punctuation, constant.numeric, entity.name.type, entity.other.attribute-name, variable.parameter (only .function), support.type.primitive; no semanticTokenColors."
	],
